{#-
  Built-in `group_summary` template (ADR 001 D5, D10).

  The storm-collapse parent. Individual alerts are threaded underneath it and each keeps
  its own message, so per-alert resolve still edits the right child; only the visual
  placement changes.

  Receives one variable, `group`. `group.title` is the heading and is never empty: it is
  the `alertname` label, or — when `group_by` does not include one — the labels
  Alertmanager grouped on, rendered `k=v`. `group.labels` is those labels as a map.

  The "grouped by" line is only worth printing when the heading did not already say it:
  when `alertname` is the heading the other grouping labels are still news, and when
  there is no `alertname` the heading *is* the label list.
-#}
{% if group.all_resolved -%}
*:white_check_mark: RESOLVED · {{ group.total }} alerts* · {{ group.title }}
{% else -%}
*:rotating_light: FIRING · {{ group.firing }} of {{ group.total }} alerts* · {{ group.title }}
{% endif %}
{%- if group.resolved and not group.all_resolved %}
_{{ group.resolved }} already resolved_
{% endif %}
{%- if group.labels.alertname and group.labels|length > 1 %}
_grouped by_ {% for key, value in group.labels|items %}{% if key != "alertname" %}`{{ key }}={{ value }}` {% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
_Alertmanager group_ `{{ group.group_key }}`
_Each alert is threaded under this message and updated there as it resolves._
